  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oven to 425 F. Line a large rimmed baking sheet with parchment paper.",
    "Toss the potatoes on the pan with 1 tbsp olive oil, 1/4 tsp salt, and 1/4 tsp pepper. Spread them cut side down and roast for 10 minutes.",
    "Stir together the remaining 3 tbsp olive oil, garlic, lemon zest, lemon juice, oregano, paprika, 1 tsp salt, and 1/4 tsp pepper in a large bowl.",
    "Add the chicken to the bowl and turn it to coat well. Toss the green beans in the same bowl to pick up the leftover marinade.",
    "Move the potatoes to one side of the pan. Place the chicken in a single layer in the center and scatter the green beans around it.",
    "Roast for 22 to 25 minutes, until the potatoes are golden and tender and the chicken reads 165 F in the thickest part.",
    "Rest the pan for 5 minutes. Spoon the pan juices over the chicken and vegetables before serving.",
    "For leftovers, cool the food and store it in a covered container in the fridge for up to 3 days. Reheat until hot."
  ],
